/-!
# The SAGBI criterion for monic families

Let `m` be a monomial order on `σ →₀ ℕ` and let `c : ι → MvPolynomial σ k` be a family of monic
polynomials over a field, with leading exponents `a i = m.degree (c i)`. Write
`A w = ∑ i, w i • a i` (`Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a w`) for the exponent map, and `φ = aeval c`
for the substitution `Y i ↦ c i` of polynomials in variables `Y i`, `i : ι`. The image
`φ (Y^w) = ∏ i, c i ^ w i` is monic with leading exponent `A w`. Its leading term `X^(A w)` is the
image of `Y^w` under the substitution `Y i ↦ X^(a i)` of the leading monomials, whose kernel is the
toric ideal `TauCeti.toricIdeal k a`.

Choose binomials `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)` generating the toric ideal. The images of their two monomials
under `φ` have the same leading monomial `X^(A (u j))`, which cancels. The **SAGBI criterion**
states that `c` is a SAGBI basis of the subalgebra `k[c]` it generates if and only if each image
`φ (Y^(u j) - Y^(v j))` has a *bounded zero subduction*: a polynomial `Q` in the variables `Y i`
with `φ Q = φ (Y^(u j) - Y^(v j))` all of whose exponents `w` satisfy `A w ≺ A (u j)`. When the
image is zero this holds with `Q = 0`; no inequality is asserted for the degree of the zero
polynomial. The finite certificates `Q` are the input to the presentation of `k[c]` and to the
flat degeneration of `k[c]` to the semigroup algebra of its initial algebra.

## Main results

* `MonomialOrder.weightedHomogeneousComponent_mem_toricIdeal`: if all exponents `w` of `P` have
  `A w ≼ e` and the coefficient of `X^e` in `φ P` vanishes, then the part of `P` of weight `e`
  lies in the toric ideal.
* `MonomialOrder.IsSAGBIBasis.exists_aeval_eq_aeval_sub`: if `c` is a SAGBI basis of `k[c]`, then
  every binomial `Y^u - Y^v` with `A u = A v` has a bounded zero subduction.
* `MonomialOrder.linearCombination_sub_weightedHomogeneousComponent_add_sum_lt`: if every
  exponent `w` in `P.support` satisfies `A w ≼ δ`, subtracting the weight-`δ` component of `P`
  and adding combinations `∑ j, g j * Q j`, where every exponent `x` in the support of `g j`
  satisfies `A x + e j = δ` and every exponent `y` in the support of `Q j` satisfies `A y ≺ e j`,
  ensures that each product exponent has weight `A x + A y ≺ δ` and strictly lowers the weight
  bound below `δ`.
* `MonomialOrder.exists_finsupp_sum_mul_toricIdeal_eq_weightedHomogeneousComponent`: if all
  exponents `w` of `P` have `A w ≼ δ` and the coefficient of `X^δ` in `φ P` vanishes, then the
  weight-`δ` component of `P` is a combination `∑ j, g j * (Y^(u j) - Y^(v j))` with every
  exponent `x` of `g j` satisfying `A x + A (u j) = δ`.
* `MonomialOrder.exists_finsupp_forall_mem_support_sub_sum_lt`: if all exponents `w` of `P` have
  `A w ≼ δ` and the coefficient of `X^δ` in `φ P` vanishes, then subtracting a combination of the
  relations `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j) - Q j` of weight `δ` lowers the bound `δ`, for any polynomials `Q j`
  all of whose exponents `w` satisfy `A w ≺ A (u j)`.
* `MonomialOrder.exists_degree_aeval_mem_closure_of_step`: well-founded top-weight descent for
  monic family representations, shared by the SAGBI criterion and fair completion.
* `MonomialOrder.isSAGBIBasis_range_iff_forall_exists_aeval_eq`: **the SAGBI criterion**.

## Implementation notes

Sufficiency is a well-founded induction on the largest value `δ` of `A` on the exponents of a
representation `f = φ P` of a nonzero element of `k[c]`. If the coefficients of `P` at the
exponents `w` with `A w = δ` have nonzero sum, then `f` has leading exponent `δ`, which lies in
the monoid generated by the `a i`. Otherwise the part of `P` of weight `δ` lies in the toric
ideal. The weight-`δ` component of its expression through the generating binomials is a sum of
multiples of the binomials of weight exactly `δ`, and replacing each binomial by its bounded zero
subduction gives a representation of `f` with smaller `δ`.

## References

* B. Sturmfels, *Gröbner Bases and Convex Polytopes*, University Lecture Series 8, AMS, 1996,
  Chapter 11.
* L. Robbiano, M. Sweedler, *Subalgebra bases*, in *Commutative Algebra (Salvador, 1988)*,
  Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1430, Springer, 1990, 61–87.
* Bruns, Conca, Lembo, arXiv:2504.10019, §2, Theorem 2.2 and Proposition 2.4, for monic SAGBI
  families and bounded subduction.
-/

public section

open MvPolynomial

namespace MonomialOrder

variable {σ ι : Type*} {m : MonomialOrder σ}

section CommSemiring

variable {R : Type*} [CommSemiring R] {c : ι → MvPolynomial σ R}

/-- Let `c` be a monic family and write `A w = ∑ i, w i • m.degree (c i)`. If every exponent `w` of
`P` satisfies `A w ≼ δ` and the coefficient of `X^δ` in `aeval c P` vanishes, then the part of `P`
of weight `δ` for the weights `m.degree (c i)` lies in the toric ideal of the leading exponents of
`c`: the cancelling top part of `P` is a relation among the leading monomials. -/
theorem weightedHomogeneousComponent_mem_toricIdeal (hc : ∀ i, m.Monic (c i))
    {P : MvPolynomial ι R} {δ : σ →₀ ℕ}
    (hP : ∀ w ∈ P.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≼[m] δ)
    (hδ : (aeval c P).coeff δ = 0) :
    weightedHomogeneousComponent (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) δ P ∈
      TauCeti.toricIdeal R (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) := by
  classical
  have hA (w : ι →₀ ℕ) : Finsupp.weight (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w =
      Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w := by
    rw [Finsupp.weight_apply, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply]
  rw [coeff_aeval_of_forall_le hc hP] at hδ
  rw [TauCeti.mem_toricIdeal_iff, weightedHomogeneousComponent_apply, map_sum]
  simp_rw [TauCeti.aeval_single_monomial, single_eq_monomial]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl (g := fun w ↦ monomial δ (P.coeff w)) fun w hw ↦ by
    rw [← hA, (Finset.mem_filter.1 hw).2], ← map_sum]
  simp only [hA]
  rw [hδ, map_zero]

/-- **Well-founded SAGBI descent.** Given a family of monic polynomial families `c s` indexed by
stages `s : α` and a top-weight reduction step replacing any vanishing top-weight representation
at stage `s` with a representation of the same polynomial at some stage `s'` with strictly smaller
support weights, the leading exponent of any nonzero `aeval (c s₀) P₀` lies in the additive
submonoid generated by the leading exponents of some stage `s`. -/
theorem exists_degree_aeval_mem_closure_of_step {α : Type*} {ι : α → Type*}
    {c : ∀ s, ι s → MvPolynomial σ R} (hc : ∀ s i, m.Monic (c s i))
    (hstep : ∀ {s : α} {P : MvPolynomial (ι s) R} {δ : σ →₀ ℕ},
      (∀ w ∈ P.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c s i)) w ≼[m] δ) →
      (aeval (c s) P).coeff δ = 0 →
      ∃ s' : α, ∃ P' : MvPolynomial (ι s') R,
        aeval (c s') P' = aeval (c s) P ∧
        ∀ w ∈ P'.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c s' i)) w ≺[m] δ)
    {s₀ : α} {P₀ : MvPolynomial (ι s₀) R} (hP₀ : aeval (c s₀) P₀ ≠ 0) :
    ∃ s : α, m.degree (aeval (c s₀) P₀) ∈
      AddSubmonoid.closure (Set.range fun i ↦ m.degree (c s i)) := by
  classical
  have key : ∀ (δ : σ →₀ ℕ) (s : α) (P : MvPolynomial (ι s) R),
      aeval (c s) P = aeval (c s₀) P₀ →
      (∀ w ∈ P.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c s i)) w ≼[m] δ) →
      ∃ s' : α, m.degree (aeval (c s₀) P₀) ∈
        AddSubmonoid.closure (Set.range fun i ↦ m.degree (c s' i)) := by
    intro δ
    induction hd : m.toSyn δ using WellFoundedLT.induction generalizing δ with
    | ind d ih =>
      subst hd
      intro s P hPf hPδ
      by_cases htop : (aeval (c s) P).coeff δ = 0
      · -- The top-weight coefficients cancel; invoke `hstep` to strictly lower the weight bound.
        obtain ⟨s', P', hP'P, hlt⟩ := hstep hPδ htop
        have hP'f : aeval (c s') P' = aeval (c s₀) P₀ := hP'P.trans hPf
        have hne : P'.support.Nonempty :=
          support_nonempty.2 fun h0 ↦ hP₀ (by rw [← hP'f, h0, map_zero])
        obtain ⟨w₀, hw₀, hmax⟩ := Finset.exists_max_image _
          (fun w ↦ m.toSyn (Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c s' i)) w)) hne
        exact ih _ (hlt w₀ hw₀) _ rfl s' P' hP'f hmax
      · -- Otherwise the leading exponent of `aeval (c s₀) P₀` is `δ`, a value of `A`.
        have hdeg : m.degree (aeval (c s₀) P₀) = δ := by
          rw [← hPf]
          exact m.toSyn.injective <| le_antisymm (degree_aeval_le_of_forall_le hPδ)
            (m.le_degree (mem_support_iff.2 htop))
        rw [coeff_aeval_of_forall_le (hc s) hPδ] at htop
        obtain ⟨w, hw, -⟩ := Finset.exists_ne_zero_of_sum_ne_zero htop
        refine ⟨s, ?_⟩
        rw [hdeg, ← (Finset.mem_filter.1 hw).2]
        exact AddSubmonoid.mem_closure_range_iff.2 ⟨w, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply ℕ w⟩
  have hne : P₀.support.Nonempty := support_nonempty.2 fun h0 ↦ hP₀ (by rw [h0, map_zero])
  obtain ⟨w₀, -, hmax⟩ := Finset.exists_max_image _
    (fun w ↦ m.toSyn (Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c s₀ i)) w)) hne
  exact key _ s₀ P₀ rfl hmax

end CommSemiring

section Ring

variable {R J : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- **Support-weight bound after subtracting a top-weight component.** If every exponent `w` of `P`
satisfies `A w ≼ δ` for the additive weight `A = Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a`, every exponent `x`
of `g j` satisfies `A x + e j = δ`, and every exponent `y` of `Q j` satisfies `A y ≺ e j`, then
every exponent `w` of `(P - weightedHomogeneousComponent a δ P) + ∑ j, g j * Q j` satisfies
`A w ≺ δ`. -/
theorem linearCombination_sub_weightedHomogeneousComponent_add_sum_lt
    (a : ι → σ →₀ ℕ) (e : J → σ →₀ ℕ)
    {P : MvPolynomial ι R} {δ : σ →₀ ℕ} {g : J →₀ MvPolynomial ι R} {Q : J → MvPolynomial ι R}
    (hPδ : ∀ w ∈ P.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a w ≼[m] δ)
    (hg : ∀ j ∈ g.support, ∀ x ∈ (g j).support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a x + e j = δ)
    (hQ : ∀ j ∈ g.support, ∀ y ∈ (Q j).support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a y ≺[m] e j)
    {w : ι →₀ ℕ}
    (hw : w ∈ (P - weightedHomogeneousComponent a δ P + g.sum fun j q ↦ q * Q j).support) :
    Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a w ≺[m] δ := by
  classical
  have hsyn (u : ι →₀ ℕ) :
      Finsupp.weight (m.toSyn ∘ a) u = m.toSyn (Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a u) :=
    Finsupp.weight_comp_eq_apply_linearCombination m.toSyn.toAddMonoidHom a u
  have hwhc : weightedHomogeneousComponent a δ P =
      weightedHomogeneousComponent (m.toSyn ∘ a) (m.toSyn δ) P := by
    ext u
    simp only [coeff_weightedHomogeneousComponent, hsyn, Finsupp.weight_apply,
      Finsupp.linearCombination_apply, m.toSyn.injective.eq_iff]
    congr 1
  rw [hwhc] at hw
  simpa [hsyn] using weight_sub_weightedHomogeneousComponent_add_sum_lt
    (m.toSyn ∘ a) (m.toSyn ∘ e) (fun u hu ↦ by simpa [hsyn] using hPδ u hu)
    (fun j hj x hx ↦ by simpa [hsyn, ← map_add] using congrArg m.toSyn (hg j hj x hx))
    (fun j hj y hy ↦ by simpa [hsyn] using hQ j hj y hy) hw

end Ring

section CommRing

variable {R J : Type*} [CommRing R] [Nontrivial R] {c : ι → MvPolynomial σ R}

/-- **Top-weight toric decomposition** for a monic family `c`. Write
`A w = ∑ i, w i • m.degree (c i)` and let binomials `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)` generate the toric ideal
of the leading exponents of `c`. If every exponent `w` of `P` satisfies `A w ≼ δ` and the
coefficient of `X^δ` in `aeval c P` vanishes, then the weight-`δ` component of `P` is a
combination `∑ j, g j * (Y^(u j) - Y^(v j))` in which every exponent `x` of `g j` satisfies
`A x + A (u j) = δ`. -/
theorem exists_finsupp_sum_mul_toricIdeal_eq_weightedHomogeneousComponent (hc : ∀ i, m.Monic (c i))
    {u v : J → ι →₀ ℕ}
    (hJ : TauCeti.toricIdeal R (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ monomial (u j) (1 : R) - monomial (v j) 1))
    {P : MvPolynomial ι R} {δ : σ →₀ ℕ}
    (hPδ : ∀ w ∈ P.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≼[m] δ)
    (hδ : (aeval c P).coeff δ = 0) :
    ∃ g : J →₀ MvPolynomial ι R,
      (g.sum fun j q ↦ q * (monomial (u j) (1 : R) - monomial (v j) 1)) =
        weightedHomogeneousComponent (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) δ P ∧
      ∀ j, ∀ x ∈ (g j).support,
        Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) x +
          Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) (u j) = δ := by
  classical
  set a := fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)
  set A := Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a
  have hA (w : ι →₀ ℕ) : Finsupp.weight a w = A w := by
    rw [Finsupp.weight_apply, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply]
  -- The generating binomial `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)` is weighted homogeneous of weight `A (u j)`.
  have hβ (j : J) :
      (monomial (u j) (1 : R) - monomial (v j) 1).IsWeightedHomogeneous a (A (u j)) := by
    have huv : A (u j) = A (v j) := TauCeti.linearCombination_eq_of_toricIdeal_eq_span hJ j
    exact (isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial _ _ _ (hA _)).sub
      (isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial _ _ _ ((hA _).trans huv.symm))
  -- The part `P₀` of `P` of weight `δ` lies in the toric ideal, so `P₀ = ∑ j, g j * β j` for some
  -- `g j` all of whose exponents `x` satisfy `A x + A (u j) = δ`.
  obtain ⟨g, hgP₀, hgA⟩ := exists_finsupp_sum_mul_eq_weightedHomogeneousComponent hβ
    (hJ ▸ weightedHomogeneousComponent_mem_toricIdeal hc hPδ hδ) δ
  rw [weightedHomogeneousComponent_eq_self
    (weightedHomogeneousComponent_isWeightedHomogeneous _ _)] at hgP₀
  refine ⟨g, hgP₀, fun j x hx ↦ ?_⟩
  simpa only [hA] using hgA j x hx

/-- **The reduction step** for a monic family `c`. Write `A w = ∑ i, w i • m.degree (c i)`, let
binomials `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)` generate the toric ideal of the leading exponents of `c`, and let
`Q j` be polynomials all of whose exponents `w` satisfy `A w ≺ A (u j)`. If every exponent `w` of
`P` satisfies `A w ≼ δ` and the coefficient of `X^δ` in `aeval c P` vanishes, then `P` is the sum
of a combination `∑ j, g j * (Y^(u j) - Y^(v j) - Q j)`, every exponent `x` of `g j` satisfying
`A x + A (u j) = δ`, and of a polynomial all of whose exponents `w` satisfy `A w ≺ δ`. -/
theorem exists_finsupp_forall_mem_support_sub_sum_lt (hc : ∀ i, m.Monic (c i))
    {u v : J → ι →₀ ℕ}
    (hJ : TauCeti.toricIdeal R (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ monomial (u j) (1 : R) - monomial (v j) 1))
    {Q : J → MvPolynomial ι R}
    (hQ : ∀ j, ∀ w ∈ (Q j).support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≺[m]
      Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) (u j))
    {P : MvPolynomial ι R} {δ : σ →₀ ℕ}
    (hPδ : ∀ w ∈ P.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≼[m] δ)
    (hδ : (aeval c P).coeff δ = 0) :
    ∃ g : J →₀ MvPolynomial ι R,
      (∀ j, ∀ x ∈ (g j).support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) x +
        Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) (u j) = δ) ∧
      ∀ w ∈ (P - g.sum fun j q ↦ q * (monomial (u j) 1 - monomial (v j) 1 - Q j)).support,
        Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≺[m] δ := by
  classical
  set a := fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)
  set A := Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a
  obtain ⟨g, hgP₀, hgA⟩ :=
    exists_finsupp_sum_mul_toricIdeal_eq_weightedHomogeneousComponent hc hJ hPδ hδ
  refine ⟨g, hgA, fun w hw ↦ ?_⟩
  -- `P - ∑ j, g j * (β j - Q j) = (P - P₀) + ∑ j, g j * Q j`.
  have heq : P - (g.sum fun j q ↦ q * (monomial (u j) 1 - monomial (v j) 1 - Q j)) =
      P - weightedHomogeneousComponent a δ P + g.sum fun j q ↦ q * Q j := by
    have hsub : (g.sum fun j q ↦ q * (monomial (u j) 1 - monomial (v j) 1 - Q j)) =
        (g.sum fun j q ↦ q * (monomial (u j) 1 - monomial (v j) 1)) - g.sum fun j q ↦ q * Q j := by
      rw [← Finsupp.sum_sub]
      simp only [mul_sub]
    rw [hsub, hgP₀]
    ring
  rw [heq] at hw
  exact linearCombination_sub_weightedHomogeneousComponent_add_sum_lt a (fun j ↦ A (u j))
    hPδ (fun j _ ↦ hgA j) (fun j _ ↦ hQ j) hw

end CommRing

section Field

variable {k J : Type*} [Field k] {c : ι → MvPolynomial σ k}

/-- **Necessity in the SAGBI criterion.** Let `c` be a monic family which is a SAGBI basis of the
subalgebra it generates, and write `A w = ∑ i, w i • m.degree (c i)`. If `A u = A v`, then the image
of `Y^u - Y^v` under `aeval c` is the image of a polynomial `Q` all of whose exponents `w` satisfy
`A w ≺ A u`. -/
theorem IsSAGBIBasis.exists_aeval_eq_aeval_sub (hc : ∀ i, m.Monic (c i))
    (h : m.IsSAGBIBasis (Set.range c) (Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range c))) {u v : ι →₀ ℕ}
    (huv : Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) u =
      Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) v) :
    ∃ Q : MvPolynomial ι k, aeval c Q = aeval c (monomial u (1 : k) - monomial v 1) ∧
      ∀ w ∈ Q.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≺[m]
        Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) u := by
  have hf : aeval c (monomial u (1 : k) - monomial v 1) ∈
      Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range c) := by
    rw [← aeval_range]
    exact AlgHom.mem_range_self _ _
  simpa only [Function.comp_def] using
    h.exists_aeval_eq_support_lt (fun i ↦ (hc i).ne_zero) hf
      (m.aeval_monomial_sub_monomial_eq_zero_or_degree_lt hc u v
        (by simpa only [Function.comp_def] using huv))

/-- **The SAGBI criterion.** Let `c` be a family of monic polynomials over a field, write
`A w = ∑ i, w i • m.degree (c i)`, and let binomials `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)` generate the toric ideal
of the leading exponents of `c`. Then `c` is a SAGBI basis of the subalgebra it generates if and
only if, for every `j`, the image of `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)` under `aeval c` is the image of a
polynomial all of whose exponents `w` satisfy `A w ≺ A (u j)`. -/
theorem isSAGBIBasis_range_iff_forall_exists_aeval_eq (hc : ∀ i, m.Monic (c i))
    {u v : J → ι →₀ ℕ}
    (hJ : TauCeti.toricIdeal k (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ monomial (u j) (1 : k) - monomial (v j) 1)) :
    m.IsSAGBIBasis (Set.range c) (Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range c)) ↔
      ∀ j, ∃ Q : MvPolynomial ι k,
        aeval c Q = aeval c (monomial (u j) (1 : k) - monomial (v j) 1) ∧
        ∀ w ∈ Q.support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) w ≺[m]
          Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) (u j) := by
  refine ⟨fun h j ↦ h.exists_aeval_eq_aeval_sub hc ?_, fun hQ ↦ ?_⟩
  · exact TauCeti.linearCombination_eq_of_toricIdeal_eq_span hJ j
  refine isSAGBIBasis_iff_degree_mem_closure.2 ⟨Algebra.subset_adjoin, fun f hf hf0 ↦ ?_⟩
  rw [Algebra.adjoin_range_eq_range_aeval] at hf
  obtain ⟨P, rfl⟩ := hf
  choose Q hQc hQlt using hQ
  obtain ⟨_, hmem⟩ := exists_degree_aeval_mem_closure_of_step (α := Unit) (ι := fun _ ↦ ι)
    (c := fun _ ↦ c) (fun _ ↦ hc) (fun {_ P δ} hPδ htop ↦ by
      obtain ⟨g, -, hlt⟩ := exists_finsupp_forall_mem_support_sub_sum_lt hc hJ hQlt hPδ htop
      exact ⟨(), P - g.sum fun j q ↦ q * (monomial (u j) 1 - monomial (v j) 1 - Q j),
        by simp [Finsupp.sum, hQc], hlt⟩)
    (s₀ := ()) hf0
  refine AddSubmonoid.closure_mono ?_ hmem
  rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨c i, ⟨⟨i, rfl⟩, (hc i).ne_zero⟩, rfl⟩

end Field

end MonomialOrder
